Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.070 align:start position:0%
 
the  2668 billionaires on forbes 2022 world's  billionaires list have established their  fortunes in all sorts of ways  building pet food and soy sauce brands  mining copper and zinc making eyeglasses  and developing real estate empires some  created new riches some inherited old  ones  these are the industries that minted the  most billionaires in 2022 as well as the  richest person in each of the ten  categories  this year the industry with the most  billionaires is finance and investments  with 393 billionaires nearly 15 percent  of the list that's an increase from last  year when finance and investments was  also the top industry with 371 list  members the sector encompasses hedge  fund and private equity tycoons  traditional bankers and fintech founders  money managers venture capitalists and  billionaires who've made investments in  a variety of sectors  the richest in this industry warren  buffett ceo of investing conglomerate  berkshire hathaway is now worth an  estimated 118 billion dollars 22 billion  dollars more than last year and the  fifth richest person in the world others  rising in finance are not yet household  names  chan pen zhao known as cz is the second  richest person in finance on this year's  list  cz founded cryptocurrency exchange  binance which has grown to become one of  the world's largest  it's been a year plagued by supply chain  slowdowns including the high profile  sinkings of more than one cargo ship but  manufacturing follows finance and  investment as the second highest  industry for billionaires with 337  demand from consumers and businesses for  goods didn't slow helping manufacturing  to mint 36 new billionaires the richest  of the pack is he shinjang the founder  of appliance maker media group the  technology industry lauded for driving  innovation globally accounts for 332  billionaires making it the third largest  industry this year down one from last  year tech fortunes from the early  internet era still hold the top spots  today the 10 biggest fortunes from tech  are from the founders of companies like  google oracle and microsoft all launched  decades ago but no one is more rich than  amazon's jeff bezos forbes previously  categorized social media tycoons as  being from the tech industry but this  year we have shifted the founders of  facebook instagram pinterest snapchat  and tick tock parent bite dance to the  media and entertainment industry to  better reflect how those companies are  functioning next up were retailers with  250 tycoons who got rich from a mix of  businesses including luxury brands  sportswear companies and grocery chains  bayonna arno remains at the top worth an  estimated 158 billion dollars as head of  luxury conglomerate lvmh which owns  brands like hennessey and louis vuitton  falguni nair india's richest self-made  woman joins the list at an estimated 4.5  billion dollars after building beauty  and fashion retailer nika which went  public last november healthcare ranks  fifth on our industry list with 217  billionaires cyrus punawala is the  richest in this category with a net  worth of 24.3 billion dollars  he is the founder of serum institute of  india the world's largest vaccine maker  by doses jeff tangni is the top newcomer  worth an estimated 2.4 billion dollars  after founding doximeter a social  platform for doctors that went public  last june  the food and beverage industry also  accounts for eight percent of the  world's billionaires  the richest in this category is zhang  chan chan who has a net worth of 65.7  billion dollars he's the chairman of  bottled water company ngfu spring and he  also controls the publicly listed  beijing wontai biological pharmacy  real estate ranks number seven with 193  billionaires china's li xiaoki is the  wealthiest within the industry before he  co-founded property development company  sun hong kai he started henderson land  development which makes up the majority  of his wealth there are 180 billionaires  whose fortunes come from diversified  holdings the wealthiest of these being  mukesh ambani the chairman of reliance  industries the firm holds interests in  petrochemicals oil and gas retail and  telecommunications only four percent of  the list falls under media and  entertainment former mayor of new york  and presidential candidate michael  bloomberg stands out with a net worth of  82 billion dollars he co-founded  financial information and media company  bloomberg lp and the sector coming in at  number 10 is energy only 95 of the  world's billionaires work within the  industry but fan hung way of china leads  the pack with a net worth of 18.2  billion dollars  she's the chair of fiber supplier henley  petrochemical which makes polyester and  textiles  while glamorous industries like sports  media and entertainment can mint many  millionaire athletes actors and  producers those whose fortune rise to  the billions are usually the select few  with ownership stakes in lucrative  brands and companies the sports industry  has three new billionaires this year  including red sox chairman tom werner  and arizona diamondback's managing  general partner ken kendrick but out of  the 27 billionaires in sports only one  was a professional athlete michael  jordan who is worth an estimated 1.7  billion dollars thanks to his stake in  the charlotte hornets  you

